{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision on `72ff1c47`: held for the owner. I read the whole report\nof `425637e6`. It is right, and two sentences of `65fb1ad0` were\nwrong.\n\n1. Item 7 of `65fb1ad0` said no export and no kernel part. The source\n   does not allow that. A split of `judgeGrant` and a body input with\n   no freshness proof change `packages/derive`. Section 7 of\n   `docs/kernel.md` holds such a head, and the E1 export needed the\n   owner's decision. I ask the owner for one exception of the same\n   form. I name no existing route, because none exists.\n2. The shape that I put to the owner is yours:\n   - One pure value check in `grant.ts`, shared with `judgeGrant`.\n     It keeps the present order: membership, key and revocation\n     first, the guards of the use next, the other value checks last.\n   - One grant value for the body with no `fresh`, and with `issued`\n     at the actual membership head. Each row of `observes` stays\n     `unavailable`.\n   - `Grant` of the contract, the runtime, the replay and\n     `predictionGrant` do not change.\n   - The condition of E1 applies: the runtime and the replay give\n     unchanged answers on the corpus.\n3. Item 1 of `65fb1ad0` chose a membership replica. Your answers a\n   and c give its cost: admission of a native pin, a private owner\n   operation, a registry, and a whole membership journal with no cap\n   on memory. I do not choose it before a second source is compared.\n4. The second source: `issueSession` runs `standingOf` for the\n   signer's key at the membership head\n   (`packages/scope/src/sessions.ts:389`). The answer could carry\n   that observation and its head beside the claims. The cost is one\n   member of `SessionAnswer` in the contract. The value is bounded,\n   and it is up to 600 seconds old.\n\nOne more source check, in the same audit lane and with no hurry.\nSend one act.\n\ne. For the second source, name each holder of a member session that\n   would explore: the page, the MCP server and the command line. Say\n   if each reads the answer of `issueSession` itself or only a\n   cached token. Say what tells an instance that its standing\n   changed before the session ends. Say what a reader must check on\n   the observation, since no journal checks it.\n\nE2 and E3 stay held. LS-5, E4 and C4 keep their order. Nothing of\nthis changes C4.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}